@voice tran-chloe
// Writer-commons, batch 0 (draft 2). Chloe Tran: comms rating, day, Bunk 1 berth 2. Off Sunday and Monday. Roster:
// reliable, dry humour; early-to-bed, lingers-at-meals. Sorts the ship's messages and sneaks a look at the gossip (with
// Zofia Santos). Bakes on rest days, if Brennan allows it (one oven at a time, inspected); quietly in charge of a
// lost-property box (one of four). No pronouns in facts.md: "Chloe" or "they".
//
// HOW THEY TALK: dry, reliable, unhurried. Says "lights out" at ten and means it. The voice of reason in Bunk 1,
// with a deadpan edge. Puts down Zofia's gossip and then asks for the rest of it.
// WITH YOU: a bunkmate: knows where your sock went (the lost-property box).
// WHAT THEY NOTICE: the time; crumbs (Brennan's inspection); lost things; whether you've eaten the last of the bake.
// MOOD TELLS: happy = bakes. Low = early to bed, earlier. Tired = "lights out" at half nine.
// NEVER: late; stays up past ten.
// RUNNING: "Lights out."; Brennan's oven inspections; the lost-property box (Chloe's, the only one, obviously).
tpl: dry
talk: Dry, reliable, unhurried; the voice of reason in Bunk 1 with a deadpan edge; "lights out" at ten; disapproves of gossip, then asks for the rest.
cares: Bunk 1 getting its sleep | the rest-day bake passing Brennan's inspection | the lost-property box | the messages going out on time
jokes: "Lights out." at ten sharp | Brennan inspects every bake | disapproves of Zofia's gossip, then asks how it ends
hi: Oh, hi | Hey | You're back
bye: Lights out at ten | Night, when it comes | See you
yes: Fine | Sure | If I must
thanks: Ta | Thanks, you
wow: Huh. Not bad | Oh, nice
sigh: Honestly
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: practical
openness: normal
loves: sweet
likes: tea | book
invites: film
joy: a rest-day bake that passes Brennan's inspection
thread: homesick
keepsake: the recipe for the bake that passed, Brennan's tick on it
avoid: gossip that isn't kind
